From 4f8dde1c3fca76281bfe1e8045ce120857c4d126 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 10:43:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add an opaque document bucket so a client app can keep its
 own documents

Bridge phase 3 (Atelier's docs/roadtrip-persistence.md, P2): a Road Trip
kept on this instance resumes from another device. Winnow stores JSON it
never reads.

- Migration 0041: app_documents (app, id) PK, user_id NOT NULL -> users ON
  DELETE CASCADE, kind, version, doc JSONB, etag; one owner index. Retention
  stated in the file: owner gestures only, no janitor.
- lib/appDocuments.ts holds every rule; the two routes under
  api/apps/[app]/docs map outcomes to status codes. Ownership is a column:
  every query carries user_id, a foreign row answers 404 (never 403), so its
  existence is not revealed. Writes need If-Match; stale or missing on an
  existing row is a 412 carrying the current revision and the client
  decides. The etag is checked again in the UPDATE's WHERE so two racing
  devices cannot both succeed. 1 MiB body cap (413), application/json
  required (415) so the browser preflights and only an allowlisted origin
  passes.
- authz: /api/apps joins the self-service prefixes, any signed-in role owns
  its documents without gaining a library write.
- capabilities: documents = { bucket: true, kinds, maxBytes }; fields added,
  no API_VERSION bump.
- README route table + docs/memory/database.md entry.

Verified: typecheck and build. migrate could not run in the authoring
container (no Postgres); run it before merging.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
